---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import OriginalIndex from '../components/OriginalIndex.astro';
import Diagram from '../components/Diagram.astro';
import ResponsiveSystemDiagram from '../components/ResponsiveSystemDiagram.astro';
import { href, sourceUrl } from '../lib/constants.mjs';
import walkthroughs from '../data/walkthroughs.json';

const firstRequestStep = walkthroughs.request[0].id;

const indexEntries = [
  { id: 'overview', label: 'Overview', description: 'One AI coordinator, clear service boundaries' },
  { id: 'knowledge-backbone', label: 'Knowledge Backbone', description: 'Retained sources, bounded model context' },
  { id: 'request-path', label: 'Request workflow', description: 'Coordination handles inference and retrieval' },
  { id: 'system-map', label: 'Architecture', description: 'Browser UI, gateway, retrieval, and state' },
  { id: 'model-routing', label: 'Models and orchestration', description: 'Delegate tasks, select inference, combine results' },
  { id: 'manual-ingestion', label: 'Ingestion', description: 'Preparation runs outside the conversation' },
  { id: 'decisions-tradeoffs', label: 'Decisions', description: 'Tradeoffs and the decisions route' }
];
---
<SiteLayout title="Architecture — Nora SuperIntelligence Lab" description="System architecture for Nora SuperIntelligence Lab’s AI agent harness: Browser UI, Coordination, and MCP gateway with clear service boundaries." path="/architecture/" customIndex={true}>
  <section class="hero" id="overview" data-index-label="Overview">
    <div class="hero-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="hero-glow hero-glow--one" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="hero-glow hero-glow--two" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="shell hero-layout">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>One AI coordinator. Clear service boundaries.</h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">Architecture shows the reusable system: who owns each responsibility, how a request moves, and why document preparation stays outside the conversation. The walkthrough applies those same boundaries to concrete scenarios.</p>
        <ul class="hero-signals" aria-label="Design principles">
          <li>Single coordinator</li>
          <li>Prepared knowledge</li>
          <li>Durable state</li>
          <li>Provider-flexible</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="hero-actions hero-actions--foundation">
          <a class="button button--primary" href={href(`/walkthroughs/?flow=request&step=${firstRequestStep}`)}>Follow the request path <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          <a class="button button--ghost" href={sourceUrl('README.md')} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Public harness on GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <OriginalIndex tagline="Architecture" entries={indexEntries} ariaLabel="Architecture navigation" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section workflow-section" id="knowledge-backbone" data-index-label="Knowledge Backbone" aria-labelledby="knowledge-backbone-heading">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading section-heading--split">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">Knowledge Backbone</p>
          <h2 id="knowledge-backbone-heading">Retained knowledge, bounded context.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>A model request has a finite context window. Prepared source text and its searchable index persist outside that window; Retrieval MCP selects the relevant passages for each task. The corpus can grow independently of a conversation, while retrieval quality determines what reaches the model.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="diagram-figure--component" aria-labelledby="knowledge-backbone-heading">
        <Diagram
          showTitle={false}
          previewSrc="/diagrams/02-question-to-answer-preview.svg"
          title="Knowledge Backbone"
          htmlUrl="/diagrams/02-question-to-answer.html"
          alt="Ingestion prepares matching text and index releases; Retrieval MCP uses shared BGE to find and read evidence for a bounded model request."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section workflow-section" id="request-path" data-index-label="Workflow">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading section-heading--split">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">Request workflow</p>
          <h2 id="request-path-heading">How one request reaches an answer.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>The MCP Gateway provides tool access; the MCP Server exposes ask_nis; the AI Coordinator performs the work. It retrieves evidence, selects inference, checks the answer and retains a checkpoint. The Browser UI reaches the same Coordination operation directly through HTTP/AG-UI.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="diagram-figure--component" aria-labelledby="request-path-heading">
        <Diagram
          showTitle={false}
          previewSrc="/diagrams/architecture-request-path-preview.svg"
          title="Request path"
          htmlUrl="/diagrams/architecture-request-path.html"
          alt="Architecture request path diagram"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section workflow-section" id="system-map" data-index-label="Architecture" aria-labelledby="system-map-heading">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading section-heading--split">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">Technical architecture</p>
          <h2 id="system-map-heading">Components, state, and system boundaries.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>The Coordination Layer groups the AI Coordinator and its interfaces. The Coordination service hosts Deep Agents/LangGraph and FastMCP; retrieval, inference, evaluation and conversation state have separate responsibilities.</p>
      </div>
      <ResponsiveSystemDiagram>
        <div class="diagram-figure--component" aria-labelledby="system-map-heading">
          <Diagram
            showTitle={false}
            title="System architecture"
            previewSrc="/diagrams/01-system-architecture-preview.svg"
            htmlUrl="/diagrams/01-system-architecture.html"
            alt="System architecture connecting browser and MCP clients to one AI Coordinator, specialist work, model routes, retained knowledge, evaluation and conversation state."
          />
        </div>
      </ResponsiveSystemDiagram>
      <p class="architecture-version"><a href={sourceUrl('docs/architecture/architecture-concept.md')}>Read the published architecture</a> for component contracts and boundaries.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section workflow-section" id="model-routing" data-index-label="Models and orchestration" aria-labelledby="model-routing-heading">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading section-heading--split">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">Models and orchestration</p>
          <h2 id="model-routing-heading">Assign the work. Select the inference.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Orchestration chooses the workflow, delegates bounded tasks and synthesizes their results. Model routing chooses suitable inference for each step: simple, general, reasoning or specialized. Ollama and Fireworks are backends; DeepSeek is a model family. Required capability and quality come before cost and latency assumptions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="diagram-figure--component" aria-labelledby="model-routing-heading">
        <Diagram
          showTitle={false}
          previewSrc="/diagrams/model-routing-preview.svg"
          title="Model routing and orchestration"
          htmlUrl="/diagrams/model-routing.html"
          alt="The same AI Coordinator plans calls, selects simple, general, reasoning or specialized model routes, and combines their results."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section workflow-section" id="manual-ingestion" data-index-label="Ingestion" aria-labelledby="manual-ingestion-heading">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading section-heading--split">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">Ingestion</p>
          <h2 id="manual-ingestion-heading">Preparation stays outside the conversation.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Conversion, preparation, embedding, and import/verification are four operator-triggered jobs. They preserve originals and prepare matching text and index releases. Backups precede preparation; verification precedes activation and answer checks. Additions include retained knowledge, and rebuilds use the complete desired set.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="diagram-figure--component" aria-labelledby="manual-ingestion-heading">
        <Diagram
          showTitle={false}
          previewSrc="/diagrams/manual-ingestion-preview.svg"
          htmlUrl="/diagrams/manual-ingestion.html"
          title="Ingestion"
          alt="Ingestion pipeline diagram"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section foundation-section" id="decisions-tradeoffs" data-index-label="Decisions">
    <div class="shell foundation-layout">
      <div class="foundation-copy">
        <p class="section-label">Decisions &amp; tradeoffs</p>
        <h2>Architecture decisions and tradeoffs.</h2>
        <p>Read the choices behind the system, examine the checks, or run the public source.</p>

      </div>
      <nav class="architecture-related" aria-label="Architecture related reading">
        <div id="purpose"><span id="approach-and-tradeoffs"></span><a href={href('/decisions/')}>Decisions</a><p>Accepted choices and tradeoffs.</p></div>
        <div id="example"><a href={href(`/walkthroughs/?flow=request&step=${firstRequestStep}`)}>Walkthroughs</a><p>The fictional request and separate ingestion scenario.</p></div>
        <div id="boundaries-and-recovery"><a href={href('/validation/')}>Validation</a><p>Recorded checks and their limits.</p></div>
        <div id="reference"><a href={href('/reproduce/')}>Reproduce</a><p>Commands for the pinned public source.</p></div>
        <div><a href={href('/workflows/')}>Workflows</a><p>Question answering, knowledge ingestion, and artifact review.</p></div>
        <div><a href={href('/case-study/')}>Build story</a><p>Historical architecture choices, AI-assisted work, and evidence.</p></div>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
<style>
.architecture-version {
  max-width: 70ch;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
  line-height: 1.6;
}
.architecture-related {
  max-width: 38ch;
}
.architecture-related > div + div { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
.architecture-related p {
  color: #a6bac6;
  font-size: 1rem;
  line-height: 1.7;
  margin: 0;
}
.architecture-related a {
  color: var(--color-muted-blue);
}
.architecture-related a:hover {
  color: var(--teal-light);
}
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  #system-map .section-heading { gap: 20px; margin-bottom: 28px; }
}
</style>
